/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/Cac-formation.dat -- a dissociation of cacodylic acid (dimethylarsinic acid), written from the master:
      HCac  <=>  Cac + H+
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 1.78, dH1 = -3.5 kJ/mol (grade CBB)
      pK2 = 6.28, dH2 = -3.0 kJ/mol, dCp -86 J/mol/K (grade BBB)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  The master is HCac, the form a case declares; this record carries step 2 (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  The section header gives the empirical formula C2H7AsO2 (molecular weight 138.00); the line "where HL=C2H6AsO2" of the same section and of Section 8 is a misprint (it is the anion's formula).  The header formula is used.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species Cac; masters ( { ion HCac; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -1; } );
      logK25 -6.28; dH -3000; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 359, and Section 7.17, p. 261: pK2 6.28, dH2 -3.0 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
